{
  "$comment": "Pricing outcomes every runtime answers: `packages/quota-model` (TypeScript) and `packages/service` `pricing.rs` (Rust). The `anthropic_claude` catalog is a verbatim slice of the Relay's shipped catalog (`apps/relay/src/pricing-catalog.ts`, revision official-2026-09-06-1; `apps/relay/test/pricing-catalog.test.ts` keeps it verbatim): claude-opus-5 at $5 input, $0.50 cache read, $6.25 5-minute cache write, $10 1-hour cache write, $25 output per million tokens and $0.01 per web search, from https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing (verified 2026-08-23); the inferred cache-write rate is the 5-minute rate, and the `us` entry is those rates × 1.1. Its rows are what the Claude Code parser emits: `input_tokens` counts uncached, cache-read and cache-write tokens together, so the priced row's $13.7075 is 200k uncached × $5 + 3M read × $0.50 + 100k 5m × $6.25 + 50k 1h × $10 + 10k inferred × $6.25 + 400k output × $25 + 2 searches × $0.01. Every other catalog is synthetic.",
